cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "EIOPA risk-free rate extrapolation in Python"
abstract: >-
  A transparent Python implementation of EIOPA's method for deriving the Solvency II basic
  risk-free interest rate term structure from swap rates or government bond zero rates:
  constant-forward bootstrapping up to the first smoothing point, followed by extrapolation of
  forward rates from the last liquid forward rate to the ultimate forward rate. It also calculates
  the undertaking-specific volatility adjustment and the term structures after the interest rate
  risk shocks.
authors:
  - name: "Open-Source Modelling"
url: "https://qnityconsultants.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/open-source-modelling/EIOPA_constant_forward_methodology"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Solvency II
  - EIOPA
  - risk-free rate
  - yield curve
  - extrapolation
  - ultimate forward rate
  - volatility adjustment
  - actuarial
